## Modifying and Cleaning Strings

`str_replace` substitutes substrings, and `str_trim` removes whitespace from the ends.

### str_replace — Swap Text

```xiom
let text = "Hello, World!";
let new_text = str_replace(text, "World", "XIOM");  // "Hello, XIOM!"

let code = "x = 1; y = 2;";
let cleaned = str_replace(code, " ", "");  // "x=1;y=2;"
```

### str_trim — Remove Whitespace

```xiom
let messy = "   hello   ";
let clean = str_trim(messy);  // "hello"

let input = "
  text  
";
let trimmed = str_trim(input);  // "text"
```

`str_trim` removes spaces, tabs, and newlines from both ends.

### Practical Patterns

```xiom
fn normalize(s: Str) -> Str {
  let lower = str_lower(s);
  let trimmed = str_trim(lower);
  return trimmed;
}

fn sanitize_filename(name: Str) -> Str {
  let no_spaces = str_replace(name, " ", "_");
  let no_slashes = str_replace(no_spaces, "/", "_");
  return no_slashes;
}

fn clean_input(input: Str) -> Str {
  return str_trim(input);  // remove accidental whitespace
}
```

### Replace All Occurrences

```xiom
let template = "{{name}} is {{age}} years old";
let filled = str_replace(template, "{{name}}", "Alice");
let result = str_replace(filled, "{{age}}", "30");
// "Alice is 30 years old"
```

### Compare Before/After Trim

```xiom
fn is_blank(s: Str) -> Bool {
  return str_trim(s).len() == 0;
}

let a = is_blank("   ");   // true
let b = is_blank("hello");  // false
let c = is_blank("");       // true
```

